Hi everyone! 👋 
I came across the next issue while using the library
 
## The error
When I installed chalk and implemented it I got the next error
```
[Error: undefined Unable to resolve module #ansi-styles from /Users/Github/porcuSafe/node_modules/chalk/source/index.js: #ansi-styles could not be found within the project or in these directories:
  node_modules
> 1 | import ansiStyles from '#ansi-styles';
```

### How I implemented the library
```js
import chalk from 'chalk'
const originalLog = console.log;

console.log = function(...args) {
    // Check if the first argument looks like a tag
    if (typeof args[0] === 'string' && args[0].startsWith('[') && args[0].endsWith(']')) {
        let tag = args.shift(); // Remove the tag from the arguments array

        // Style the tag with Chalk
        const styledTag = chalk.cyan(tag);

        // Combine styled tag and original message
        args.unshift(styledTag);
    }

    originalLog.apply(console, args);
};
```

### The technologies used in my project
- react-native v0.73.2
- expo v50
- react v18.2.0
- typescript 5.0.4


### The Fix
So I used [patch-package](https://github.com/ds300/patch-package) to patch `chalk@5.3.0` for the project I'm working on.

Here is the diff that solved my problem:

```diff
diff --git a/node_modules/chalk/source/index.js b/node_modules/chalk/source/index.js
index 8bc993d..284bca5 100644
--- a/node_modules/chalk/source/index.js
+++ b/node_modules/chalk/source/index.js
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
-import ansiStyles from '#ansi-styles';
-import supportsColor from '#supports-color';
+import ansiStyles from './vendor/ansi-styles/index.js';
+import supportsColor from './vendor/supports-color/browser.js';
 import { // eslint-disable-line import/order
 	stringReplaceAll,
 	stringEncaseCRLFWithFirstIndex,
```

